### Discover — manual test requests (sub-projects 1 & 2)
###
### Requires the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or IntelliJ's built-in HTTP
### Client) so the `# @name` / `{{name.response.body...}}` chaining below works.
### Start the API first: `cd apps/api && bun run dev`.
### @baseUrl below assumes PORT=3004 (apps/api/.env on this box) — change it
### if yours differs (apps/api/.env.example defaults to 3000).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3004

### 1. Sign up — skip this request if the account already exists (409 is fine)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "handle": "wildan",
  "email": "wildan@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret123",
  "displayName": "Wildan"
}

### 2. Log in — captures the token every authenticated request below reuses
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "wildan@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret123"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}


### ================= Sub-project 1: Discover browse data =================

### 3. Create a community with tags
# @name createCommunity
POST {{baseUrl}}/communities
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Kelas Desain",
  "category": "Skill Digital",
  "description": "Belajar desain dari nol.",
  "tags": ["Desain", "UI", "UX"]
}

###
@slug = {{createCommunity.response.body.slug}}

### 4. Browse communities — each row carries tags/trending/price, plus the
###    site's popularTags alongside the list
GET {{baseUrl}}/communities

### 5. Filter by category
GET {{baseUrl}}/communities?category=Skill%20Digital

### 6. Search by name
GET {{baseUrl}}/communities?q=desain

### 7. Replace the community's tags — owner-only, full replace
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/communities/{{slug}}/tags
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "tags": ["desain", "belajar"]
}

### 8. Read the community back — tags reflect the PATCH above
GET {{baseUrl}}/communities/{{slug}}


### ================= Sub-project 2: Live viewer counts =================
### Starting a stream needs a streaming provider configured (MEDIAMTX_*  env
### vars) — without one, #9 answers 503, and #11/#12 have nothing to target.

### 9. Go live, publicly
# @name startStream
POST {{baseUrl}}/streams
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Ngobrol santai",
  "visibility": "public"
}

###
@streamId = {{startStream.response.body.id}}

### 10. List live streams — each row now carries viewerCount
GET {{baseUrl}}/streams

### 11. Simulate nginx's /auth-request for that stream, forwarding a viewer's
###     IP — this is what records a heartbeat. Replace webhookSecret with the
###     real MEDIAMTX_WEBHOOK_SECRET from apps/api/.env before running this.
@webhookSecret = REPLACE_WITH_MEDIAMTX_WEBHOOK_SECRET

GET {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/mediamtx/auth-request
X-Mediamtx-Secret: {{webhookSecret}}
X-Mtx-Stream-Id: {{streamId}}
X-Client-IP: 203.0.113.9
User-Agent: manual-test

### 12. Re-run #10 (GET /streams) now — viewerCount should read 1. Change
###     X-Client-IP in #11 and re-run both to watch the count grow; wait 20+
###     seconds and re-run #10 alone to watch it drop back to 0.

### 13. End the stream when you're done
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/streams/{{streamId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
